    <string name="setup_item_usage_access_desc">Lets the app see when you pick up your phone. Without it, only the fallback time triggers dose 1.</string>
    <string name="setup_item_full_screen_title">Full-screen alarm</string>
    <string name="setup_item_full_screen_desc">Lets the alarm turn the screen on over the lock screen.</string>
    <string name="setup_item_battery_title">Battery optimisation</string>
    <string name="setup_item_battery_desc">Set to \"Don\'t optimise\" so the system doesn\'t stop the app in the background.</string>
    <string name="setup_item_oneplus_title">OnePlus extras</string>
    <string name="setup_item_maps_title">Hold the alarm while driving</string>
    <string name="setup_item_maps_desc">Notification access lets the app see when Google Maps is navigating. The alarm then waits until navigation ends. Only Maps\' notifications are looked at. If Android calls it a restricted setting, first open App info › ⋮ › Allow restricted settings.</string>
    <string name="setup_item_oneplus_desc">Auto-launch, lock in Recents and sleep standby. These can\'t be detected, so you tick them off yourself.</string>

    <!-- OnePlus guide (docs/06-device-setup-oneplus.md) -->
    <string name="oneplus_title">OnePlus setup</string>
    <string name="oneplus_intro">OxygenOS kills background apps aggressively, and if it kills this app the reminders won\'t fire. Do these steps once after installing. Menu names vary slightly between OxygenOS builds; if a path doesn\'t match, use the search box in Settings.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_autolaunch_title">Auto-launch</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_autolaunch">Settings → Apps → Auto launch (or App management → PillReminder → Auto launch) → on. This lets the app start after a reboot.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_lock_title">Lock the app in Recents</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_lock">Open Recents, tap the ⋮ menu (or long-press) on PillReminder → Lock. This stops \"clear all\" from killing it.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_sleep_title">Sleep standby optimisation</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_sleep">Turn it off if present: Battery → More settings → Sleep standby optimisation → off. Also turn off any \"Deep optimisation\" or \"Advanced optimisation\" for the app.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_dnd_title">Do Not Disturb</string>
    <string name="oneplus_step_dnd">If the alarm doesn\'t vibrate or show while Do Not Disturb is on, go to Settings → Sound &amp; vibration → Do Not Disturb and allow Alarms, or add PillReminder under Apps exceptions.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_verify">Verify: run Settings → Test alarm. Then lock the phone and wait for a 1-minute test escalation. The screen should turn on with the alarm.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_after_update">After an OxygenOS update, re-check these steps and the battery setting, because updates sometimes reset them.</string>
    <string name="oneplus_open_app_settings">Open app settings</string>
    <string name="oneplus_done_checkbox">I\'ve done this</string>

